+{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1041440,"num_turns":81,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"944698db-e744-486d-8b3f-44c045ae3582","total_cost_usd":7.609833999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":103,"cache_creation_input_tokens":202075,"cache_read_input_tokens":7556488,"output_tokens":72413,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":202075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15937,"cache_read_input_tokens":217308,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":369},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":103,"outputTokens":72413,"cacheReadInputTokens":7556488,"cacheCreationInputTokens":202075,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":7.609833999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"# Critical-incremental review — plan03-1 current-review remediation\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Review kind | `critical-incremental` |\n| Plan ID | `plan03-1` |\n| Continuity base | `5b474d5c1735beb8cca922fd6cc7b6304926df2c` |\n| Frozen target | `74ecd4fb64311c69ae0d758d8c1d99b27a9c5572` |\n| Reviewer lane | protocol correctness, architecture, concurrency/persistence invariants |\n| Requested model | `claude-opus-5` |\n| Actual model | self-reported `claude-opus-5` (Opus 5) from the session environment; not independently verifiable from inside the snapshot — the coordinator must confirm from raw invocation `modelUsage` |\n| Snapshot | read-only worktree; no file, Git, job or external state was modified |\n| Other reviewer outputs | not inspected |\n\n## Scope\n\nReviewed the complete increment plus current-state context for every directly affected caller: `fs_diloco/core/config.py`, `fs_diloco/core/versions.py`, `fs_diloco/protocol/__init__.py` and the concrete protocol modules, `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer.py`, `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer_entrypoint.py`, `fs_diloco/runtime/learner_entrypoint.py`, `fs_diloco/syncer.py`, `fs_diloco/learner.py`, `fs_diloco/storage/{authority,leader_lease,paths,control,admission,atomic_io,schema.sql}`, `fs_diloco/tools/{clean_run,init_run,launch_independent_run,request_static_replacement}.py`, `fs_diloco/runtime/services/{dynamic_capacity,terminal}.py`, all three `configs/*.yaml`, `scripts/miyabi/{check_full_protocol_run,check_plan_completion,run_validation_suite}.py`, `scripts/miyabi/{run_full_protocol.pbs,run_full_protocol_allocation.sh,run_full_protocol_rank.sh,run_multi_agent_review.pbs}`, the changed and adjacent tests, `tests/module_coverage.json`, `pyproject.toml`, `README.md`, `docs/{configuration,design,operations,testing}.md`, `plans/workflow.md`, `plans/DOING/plans/plan03-1.md`, and the tracked plan03-1 report set including `artifact-schema.md`, `identity-authority.md`, `formal-ladder-manifest.json`, `workflow_state.yaml` and the tracked disposition.\n\nStatic checks I executed against the snapshot (read-only, no test suite run): the new content-scan regex over the 147 in-scope text files, the versioned-wire-type AST scan, the `tests/module_coverage.json` completeness relation, and the `check_plan_completion._manifest_workload` comparison against the tracked manifest.\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n### FSD-R1 — High / blocking — the new manifest workload key breaks the completion contract and fails registered tests\n\n**Violated invariant.** The takeover boundary must have one owner; a registered formal-ladder gate must match its Checker contract exactly.\n\n**Evidence (observed).**\n- `reports/DOING/plan03-1/formal-ladder-manifest.json:114` adds `\"syncer_takeover_boundary_version\": 2` inside the `F1-final-syncer-takeover` gate's `workload` object (`:97` is the gate id).\n- `scripts/miyabi/check_plan_completion.py:146-156` — `_manifest_workload()` for a runtime gate returns exactly six keys: `config, fault_scenario, learners, local_optimizer_steps_per_cycle, committed_global_steps, direct_weight_tokens_applied`. The key was not added to `GATE_CONTRACTS[\"F1-final-syncer-takeover\"]` (`:103-119`).\n- `scripts/miyabi/check_plan_completion.py:296` — `or gate[\"workload\"] != _manifest_workload(contract)` → `:305` `raise RuntimeError(f\"formal ladder gate registration is invalid: {gate['id']}\")`.\n- `tests/harness/test_plan_completion.py:279-282` asserts `gate[\"workload\"] == module._manifest_workload(contract)` for every gate of the **tracked** manifest.\n- I executed the exact comparison against the tracked manifest: `U1`, `F1-normal`, `F1-learner-replacement` and `G1` match; `F1-final-syncer-takeover` mismatches on the extra key.\n- `scripts/miyabi/run_validation_suite.py:22` registers `tests/harness/test_plan_completion.py` in `FOCUSED_TESTS`.\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** Run U1 on this target. `test_candidate_manifest_registers_exact_final_ladder` fails immediately. `_registered_manifest()` (`tests/harness/test_plan_completion.py:49-76`) deep-copies the tracked manifest and never rewrites `workload`, so `test_completion_aggregate_accepts_registered_staged_inputs` (`:305`) and the other tests that route through `_materialize_registered_inputs` → `_validate_registered_manifest` also fail with `formal ladder gate registration is invalid: F1-final-syncer-takeover`. If U1 were skipped, the same failure would land at FINAL-01 — after the 5-node fault scenarios and the 9-node formal gate have already been consumed.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Pick one owner and make the contract agree. Either delete `formal-ladder-manifest.json:114`, or add `\"syncer_takeover_boundary_version\": 2` to `GATE_CONTRACTS[\"F1-final-syncer-takeover\"]` and emit it from `_manifest_workload()` only when `contract[\"fault_scenario\"] == \"syncer_takeover\"`. The second option is the one consistent with FSD-M6's \"one authoritative configured value\", but it then needs the value to reach the Checker evidence (see FSD-R6).\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** A test asserting that the registered manifest's `syncer_takeover_boundary_version` equals both `GATE_CONTRACTS` and the literal exported by `scripts/miyabi/run_full_protocol.pbs` (`readonly SYNCER_TAKEOVER_BOUNDARY_VERSION=2`), so a third declaration cannot drift silently again.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R2 — Medium — the ingest whitelist makes transient SQLite failures candidate-fatal, exceeding the accepted FSD-M5 direction\n\n**Violated invariant.** Schema, command-conflict and stale-leader integrity failures must not be swallowed — but nothing in the accepted direction asks for retryable storage faults to terminate the only syncer.\n\n**Evidence (observed).**\n- `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer.py:850-852` — `except (AuthoritySchemaError, CommandConflictError, StaleLeaderTokenError): raise` then `except (MembershipFenceError, OSError, ValueError) as exc:`; `:873-875` the same with `ProposalPayloadError` added.\n- The base swallowed everything with `except Exception`. The remediation implemented the narrowing as a **whitelist**, not as a blacklist of the three named classes.\n- `fs_diloco/storage/authority.py` contains no `except sqlite3` handler; command operations propagate raw driver exceptions. I verified `sqlite3.OperationalError.__mro__` is `(OperationalError, DatabaseError, sqlite3.Error, Exception, …)` and `issubclass(sqlite3.OperationalError, (OSError, ValueError))` is `False`.\n- Two concurrent writers exist on the shared-filesystem database: the main leader connection and `_LeaseRenewer._run` (`fs_diloco/runtime/syncer_entrypoint.py:62-75`), with `business_busy_timeout_ms: 5000`.\n- `scripts/miyabi/run_full_protocol_rank.sh:161-172` — for `none` and `learner_replacement`, rank 0 runs exactly one `run_syncer`; there is no successor process.\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** During the 9-node formal run, the `INSERT INTO cycle_receipts` inside `ingest_cycle_receipt` (`fs_diloco/storage/authority.py:1336-1347`) raises `sqlite3.OperationalError: database is locked` (or `disk I/O error` on the shared FS) after the 5-second busy timeout. Previously this produced one `receipt_ingest_rejected` telemetry event and the next loop iteration re-ingested the same durable receipt file. Now it escapes `_ingest_proposals`, is caught only by the candidate error boundary (`syncer_entrypoint.py:240-256`), fences the epoch as `error`, and `run_syncer` returns nonzero — the run dies with no successor and the gate fails.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Keep the explicit `except (AuthoritySchemaError, CommandConflictError, StaleLeaderTokenError): raise` clause and restore the second clause to `except Exception as exc:` in both handlers. That implements exactly the accepted FSD-M5 wording with no collateral reclassification.\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** Inject `sqlite3.OperationalError` from a fake `ingest_cycle_receipt` and assert `_ingest_proposals` returns normally after emitting `receipt_ingest_rejected` — pairing with the propagation tests so the boundary between \"terminal integrity failure\" and \"retryable storage fault\" is pinned in both directions.\n\n*Inference, stated separately:* if the team deliberately prefers fail-fast on any storage fault, that is a defensible policy, but it is a scope change beyond the disposed finding and should be recorded as such rather than arriving as a side effect of a narrowing.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R3 — Medium — FSD-M1 is only half closed: the authorized static-replacement branch has no test anywhere\n\n**Violated invariant.** \"Static replacement admission is authorized and fenced by the real authority.\"\n\n**Evidence (observed).**\n- `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer.py:502-524` (committed-replay path) and `:536-562` (fresh-request path) call `read_static_replacement_authorization(...)` and derive `allow_logical_replacement=authorization is not None` (`:553`) and `replacement_reason=f\"operator_static_replacement:{authorization[1]}\"` (`:555`).\n- `grep -rn \"read_static_replacement_authorization\" tests/` returns **no hits**. No test in the repository exercises the positive authorization branch.\n- The new `tests/runtime/test_syncer_composition.py:44-93` covers only the negative case: a second logical launch without authorization is rejected with `MembershipFenceError` and an `admission_rejected` telemetry event. The `_ingest_proposals` tests (`:95-153`) use `SimpleNamespace` fakes for `authority` and `leader`, so they do not exercise the real authority at all.\n- `tests/tools/test_request_static_replacement.py` covers only the operator tool's collision message; `tests/storage/test_static_contributor_binding.py` covers `bind_or_replace_static_attempt` directly, below the composition that decides authorization.\n- `tests/module_coverage.json:218-222` now names `test_active_static_attempt_replacement_requires_matching_authorization` as the sole boundary owner of `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer.py`, replacing the fault-seam mapping.\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** Change `syncer.py:553` to `allow_logical_replacement=True`. Every unit, architecture and harness test in the repository still passes, including the new composition test (its request is rejected by the authority for a different reason only when `allow_logical_replacement` is `False`, so with `True` the unauthorized second logical launch is instead *admitted*, silently retiring the active generation-1 binding). The only oracle that would notice is the 5-node `learner_replacement` runtime gate, which this workflow step does not run before promotion.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Extend `tests/runtime/test_syncer_composition.py` with a positive case on the same real `LeaderAuthority` fixture: publish an authorization naming the exact old fence (`fs_diloco/storage/admission.publish_static_replacement_authorization`, the symbol the operator tool uses), run `_admit_requests`, and assert `binding_generation == 2`, `final_status == \"replaced\"` in `static_binding_history`, the `operator_static_replacement:` reason prefix, and an `outcome == \"admitted\"` disposition. Add one mutation where the authorization names a different old fence and admission is still rejected.\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** As above; this is the smallest change that makes `syncer.py:536-562` non-vacuously owned by its declared boundary test.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R4 — Low — the FSD-M5 propagation oracle only covers one of the three integrity classes\n\n**Violated invariant.** Schema and stale-leader failures must be provably non-swallowable.\n\n**Evidence (observed).** `tests/runtime/test_syncer_composition.py:95-133` and `:136-153` inject `CommandConflictError` only. No test injects `AuthoritySchemaError` or `StaleLeaderTokenError` into `ingest_cycle_receipt` / `ingest_proposal`.\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** Delete `AuthoritySchemaError` and `StaleLeaderTokenError` from both re-raise tuples at `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer.py:850` and `:873`. `AuthoritySchemaError` and `StaleLeaderTokenError` are `RuntimeError` subclasses, so they would fall through to the telemetry clause only if that clause were broadened — with the current whitelist they would escape uncaught, but the *intent* (explicit, reviewed propagation) is no longer pinned by any assertion, and under the FSD-R2 fix (`except Exception`) their removal would silently reintroduce exactly the disposed defect with a green suite.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Parametrize the two propagation tests over `(AuthoritySchemaError, CommandConflictError, StaleLeaderTokenError)`.\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** The parametrized propagation test above.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R5 — Low — FSD-L1 is only half closed: `clean_run` still hand-derives the owner epoch path\n\n**Violated invariant.** One owner for epoch-directory derivation.\n\n**Evidence (observed).**\n- Fixed: `scripts/miyabi/check_full_protocol_run.py:598-602` now calls `RunPaths(run_root).epoch_stop_path(...)`.\n- Not fixed: `fs_diloco/tools/clean_run.py:207-216` still computes `hashlib.sha256(owner_id).hexdigest()[:12]` and assembles `control/syncer_epochs/e{epoch:06d}_{owner_short}/terminal/stop_g{generation:06d}.json` by hand. This is product code, and it gates a destructive operation.\n- The single writer is `fs_diloco/storage/control.py:120` via `paths.epoch_stop_path(...)`; the canonical derivation is `fs_diloco/storage/paths.py:161-165` and `:252`.\n- `tests/test_clean_run.py:58-60` re-derives the same literal by hand, so the test and the tool agree with each other while both can drift from `RunPaths` undetected.\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** Change `RunPaths.owner_short` (`paths.py:161-162`) to 16 hex characters. The writer, the Checker and every test still agree; `python -m fs_diloco.tools.clean_run` then raises `CleanupRefusedError(\"immutable terminal control is missing\")` for every genuinely completed run, and no test fails.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Import `RunPaths` in `clean_run.py` (the `tools → storage` direction is already used at `:24` and is permitted by `tests/architecture/test_dependency_boundaries.py`) and replace `:207-216` with `RunPaths(run_root).epoch_stop_path(int(terminal[\"finalized_by_epoch\"]), str(terminal[\"finalized_by_owner_id\"]), int(terminal[\"generation\"]))`.\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** Assert in `tests/test_clean_run.py` that the path the tool consults equals `RunPaths(run).epoch_stop_path(...)`, so a layout change breaks the test rather than the tool.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R6 — Low — the takeover boundary value is not bound to durable evidence and has no discriminating oracle\n\n**Violated invariant.** \"The takeover boundary has one owner\", consumed by launcher and Checker.\n\n**Evidence (observed).**\n- Launcher chain is correct: `scripts/miyabi/run_full_protocol.pbs:28,40,57` (`readonly SYNCER_TAKEOVER_BOUNDARY_VERSION=2`, exported, passed as `--syncer-takeover-boundary-version`), `run_full_protocol_allocation.sh:12,105`, `run_full_protocol_rank.sh:177`.\n- `scripts/miyabi/check_full_protocol_run.py:850` compares the evidence's `committed_version` against the parameter, but the evidence artifact payload at `:911` records only `\"fault_scenario\"` — the validated boundary version is never written into the durable artifact.\n- `docs/testing.md:24` restates \"committed version 2\" in prose; `formal-ladder-manifest.json:114` and its `pass_formula` restate \"version-2\". These are second and third declarations with no Checker binding (and the manifest one currently breaks the contract — FSD-R1).\n- `run_full_protocol_rank.sh:5-10` does not list `SYNCER_TAKEOVER_BOUNDARY_VERSION` among its `: \"${VAR:?}\"` required variables, unlike `run_full_protocol_allocation.sh:12`. Under `set -u` an unset value fails only when the takeover branch is reached.\n- Every harness fixture uses `2` (`tests/harness/test_full_protocol_harness.py:252,358,675,694`); the only takeover mutation flips `lease_renewer_quiesced` (`:490-493`).\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** Revert `check_full_protocol_run.py:850` to the literal `!= 2` and ignore the new argument entirely. The full harness suite still passes because no fixture uses any value other than 2, and the parser test at `:694` proves only that argparse stores the value.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Add `\"syncer_takeover_boundary_version\": syncer_takeover_boundary_version` to the evidence payload at `:911`, and add `: \"${SYNCER_TAKEOVER_BOUNDARY_VERSION:?…}\"` to the rank script's required list.\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** A harness case with fixture `fault_boundary.committed_version = 3` and `--syncer-takeover-boundary-version 3` that PASSes, plus the 3-vs-2 mismatch that produces `syncer takeover evidence does not prove the registered fault layer`.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R7 — Low — the new `finally` block can replace the primary candidate failure with a release failure\n\n**Violated invariant.** Stale-leader integrity failures must surface as themselves; the epoch projection is the fault oracle.\n\n**Evidence (observed).** `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer_entrypoint.py:257-264`. `candidate_failed` is set only *after* `authority.fail_leader(token)` succeeds (`:252-253`). `release_leader` raises `StaleLeaderTokenError` via `_verify_token` (`fs_diloco/storage/authority.py:998-1002`), and it writes `final_state='released'` (`:1012`) whereas `fail_leader` writes `final_state='error'` (`:1038`).\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** `run_fenced_syncer` raises `AuthoritySchemaError` (exactly the class FSD-M5 made terminal). `authority.fail_leader(token)` at `:252` raises against the same damaged database, so `candidate_failed` stays `False` and a note is attached. The `finally` block then calls `release_leader(token)`. Two outcomes, both wrong: if it raises, that exception replaces `AuthoritySchemaError` as the propagating exception (the original survives only as `__context__`); if it succeeds, the failed candidate's epoch is durably recorded as `released` instead of `error`, corrupting the exact `syncer_epochs.final_state` tuple that `check_full_protocol_run.py:650` uses as the takeover oracle. The mislabelling path is pre-existing; the exception replacement is newly introduced by this increment.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Set `candidate_failed = True` unconditionally in the error boundary (before attempting `fail_leader`), so a candidate that entered its error path can never take the release path; and wrap the `release_leader` call so a failure is attached as a note to the in-flight exception rather than raised from `finally` — while still raising when there is no in-flight exception (which is what the new `test_successful_candidate_does_not_swallow_release_failure` pins, and which remains correct).\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** A candidate whose body raises and whose `fail_leader` also raises must propagate the body's exception type and must leave `final_state` not equal to `'released'`.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R8 — Low — two runnable module surfaces per actor remain\n\n**Violated invariant.** \"There is one current invocation surface and no compatibility facade.\"\n\n**Evidence (observed).** `fs_diloco/syncer.py:10-11` and `fs_diloco/learner.py:10-11` are the documented, launcher-used surfaces (`scripts/miyabi/run_full_protocol_rank.sh:26,162`, `run_syncer.pbs:21`, `run_learner.pbs:44`) and are pinned by `tests/architecture/test_plan_complete_dead_surfaces.py:73-88`. But `fs_diloco/runtime/syncer_entrypoint.py:267-268` and `fs_diloco/runtime/learner_entrypoint.py:166-167` also carry `if __name__ == \"__main__\": main()`, so `python -m fs_diloco.runtime.syncer_entrypoint` is a second, undocumented, untested entry.\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** An operator or future script invokes `python -m fs_diloco.runtime.syncer_entrypoint`; nothing in the repository documents, tests or forbids it, and the \"one invocation surface\" requirement that justified deleting `fs_diloco/cli.py` and `[project.scripts]` is not actually established.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** Delete the two `__main__` guards in `fs_diloco/runtime/*_entrypoint.py`.\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** Extend `test_runtime_composition_has_one_current_actor_boundary` with `assert \"__main__\" not in <entrypoint source>` for both runtime entrypoints.\n\n---\n\n### FSD-R9 — Low — one repository-content test can still pass vacuously (pre-existing)\n\n**Violated invariant.** \"Repository discovery/content tests cannot vacuously pass.\"\n\n**Evidence (observed).** `tests/architecture/test_dependency_boundaries.py:35-37` — `for path in (ROOT / \"fs_diloco/storage\").glob(\"*.py\"): assert …` with no non-empty guard. Contrast the sites this increment did fix: `tests/test_config.py:20-22` (`assert CONFIGS`), `tests/architecture/test_plan_complete_dead_surfaces.py:99` and `:126,129` (`assert tracked`, `assert text_files`), `tests/harness/test_full_protocol_harness.py:1016` (`assert pbs_scripts`), `tests/tools/test_resolve_scheduler_uncertainty.py:41-44` (resolved from `__file__`).\n\n**Concrete counterexample.** Rename `fs_diloco/storage` or run the suite from a layout where the glob returns nothing: the storage→runtime boundary check reports PASS while asserting nothing.\n\n**Smallest current-only fix.** `storage_modules = tuple((ROOT / \"fs_diloco/storage\").glob(\"*.py\")); assert storage_modules`.\n\n**Missing test / durable oracle.** The guard itself.\n\n---\n\n## Accepted items verified closed (with evidence)\n\n- **FSD-M2 — closed.** `identity-authority.md:28-35` and `:45-56` now scope stale-fence and stale-token rejection to authority unit evidence and explicitly state the sequential injection does not claim a live stale writer. This matches the harness: `run_full_protocol_rank.sh:173-205` kills the primary and only then starts the successor. The Checker's oracle is the provable negative — `check_full_protocol_run.py:661-675` asserts the successor committed and that no lower epoch committed at or above the successor's first version. `docs/testing.md:23-24` carries no live-old-writer claim.\n- **FSD-M3 — closed.** `tests/test_config.py:20-22` resolves `configs/` from `__file__` and asserts non-empty discovery; `tests/tools/test_resolve_scheduler_uncertainty.py:41-44` resolves from `__file__`.\n- **FSD-M4 — closed.** `tests/architecture/test_plan_complete_dead_surfaces.py:104-149` adds a content scan with non-empty guards. I executed both the path scan and the content regex over the in-scope roots: 147 text files, zero violations, zero path hits; the AST allowlist resolves to exactly `{CycleReceiptV1, FullUpdateProposalV2}`. The independently versioned wire types are correctly excluded from the product-generation rule; I found no current conflict and do not challenge that decision.\n- **FSD-M5 — closed in code** (see FSD-R2/R4 for scope and oracle). `syncer.py:850-852,873-875`; `AuthoritySchemaError`, `CommandConflictError`, `StaleLeaderTokenError` propagate to `syncer_entrypoint.py:240-256`, which publishes an error control record and fences the epoch as `error` — a durable terminal error, not an unbounded retry. `run_fenced_syncer` has no broad handler around its loop (`syncer.py:222-270`), so propagation is real. `MergeFenceConflict` is a dataclass disposition (`protocol/authority.py:128`), not an exception, so it is correctly absent from the tuples; `CycleReceiptV1.from_dict` / `_validation.py` raise only `ValueError` for malformed payloads, so no `KeyError` path was introduced.\n- **FSD-M7 — closed** except FSD-R8. `fs_diloco/cli.py` and `tests/test_cli.py` deleted, `[project.scripts]` removed, `fs_diloco/protocol/__init__.py` reduced to its docstring with zero remaining package-level `from …protocol import` sites, `tests/module_coverage.json` updated (I verified the manifest maps exactly the retained surface set with no missing or extra entry, `schema_version: 2`, sorted), `run_validation_suite.py` no longer references the deleted test, `docs/operations.md:62` uses the module invocation.\n- **FSD-L2 — closed.** `storage/schema.sql:52` restricts `final_state` to `('released','expired','error')`; the only writers are `authority.py:905` (`expired`/`released` on fencing), `:1012` (`released`), `:1038` (`error`). No code writes `'terminal'`. Revision 11 therefore matches the writable domain exactly, and `tests/storage/test_schema.py:66-71` asserts both directions for the static and dynamic parametrizations.\n- **FSD-L3 — closed.** `pyproject.toml:10` `>=3.13`, `:29` `target-version = \"py313\"`, `.python-version` `3.13`, all three pinned by `test_python_floor_and_public_invocation_surface_are_unique`.\n- **FSD-L4 — closed.** `core/config.py:98,108,112,120-124` defaults are now the synthetic/current values; all three tracked configs set them explicitly.\n- **FSD-L5 — closed** except FSD-R7. `syncer_entrypoint.py:257-264` no longer swallows the release failure and `authority.close()` now always runs; `tests/runtime/test_syncer_startup_admission.py:136-232` pins both. I traced the fake-object wiring (module-level `LeaderAuthority`/`ControlPublisher` resolved at call time inside `main`) and the test is sound.\n- **FSD-L6 — closed.** Static configs no longer declare `stream_pool_size`, `bootstrap_instances` or `scaling`; `_validate_source_shape` (`config.py:349-364`) rejects them at parse time with the message the new negative tests match; `_normalize_and_validate:533-537` derives both from `sync.num_learners`; `config_to_dict:343-349` strips them so the immutable resolved config round-trips through `load_config` unchanged. I verified every `scaling.*` consumer is gated on `scaling.enabled` (`runtime/services/dynamic_capacity.py:77`, `services/terminal.py:55`, `runtime/syncer.py:215`), and that the dynamic strictness `quorum_min <= desired_contributors <= quorum_max <= stream_pool_size` (`config.py:546-555`) remains **ungated**, so dynamic scaling stays strict when enabled. `check_full_protocol_run.py:409` consumes the stripped dict only through `.get(...)` and `training`/`data` keys, so the Checker is unaffected.\n- **FSD-L7 — respected.** `identity-authority.md:33-35` and `:53-55` state the unit-evidence boundary explicitly; I treated it as informational and did not raise it as a defect.\n- **FSD-H1…H4 — no regression observed.** The JUnit-count oracle in `run_validation_suite.py` and its `tests > 0, failures = errors = skipped = 0` policy are untouched (the only edit is the focused-list membership). `--fault-scenario` remains required with a closed enum and `_scenario_expectations` raises on anything unregistered (`check_full_protocol_run.py:324-331`); binding generations and history remain unconditionally pinned (`:630-660`); `contributor_progress.last_update_id` is still present and asserted (`tests/storage/test_schema.py:69`); the harness fixtures and mutations at `tests/harness/test_full_protocol_harness.py:355-500` still drive every replacement/takeover branch, updated only for the new required argument.\n- **Review-artifact invariants — satisfied.** `check_plan_completion.py:590-615` requires `review_artifact_version == 2` and no longer carries `external_review_status`; `grep` confirms no `skipped-by-user` remains in any Checker, test or workflow document. `run_multi_agent_review.pbs` owns exactly four lanes (`run_claude &` ×1, `run_opencode \\` ×3; Claude Opus 5, GLM-5.2, DeepSeek V4 Flash, MiniMax M3), with no `OPENCODE_KIMI_MODEL` and a matching negative assertion at `tests/harness/test_full_protocol_harness.py:1063`. The summary writer (`:545-625`) records `external_review_is_best_effort: True`, `actual_model: None`, `identity_verification: \"pending-coordinator-validation\"`, and emits `failed-command` / `invalid-output` for a missing or malformed lane — absence is never rendered as approval. `artifact-schema.md:83-90` and `plans/workflow.md:41-44,111-118,349-355` agree. Remaining `kimi` strings appear only in historical tracked evidence, which is correct.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe increment is substantively correct on most of the disposed items, and the schema-11, config-shape, exception-propagation and review-lane work is well targeted. It cannot be promoted as frozen because `formal-ladder-manifest.json:114` breaks the completion contract and fails registered tests that are in the U1 focused suite (FSD-R1), and because two accepted findings — FSD-M1's authorization branch (FSD-R3) and FSD-M5's blast radius (FSD-R2) — are not actually closed by the evidence present in the target.\n\nVerdict: CHANGES_REQUIRED","ttft_ms":2737,"ttft_stream_ms":1772,"time_to_request_ms":151,"type":"result","duration_ms":1054987,"uuid":"e36bf9ee-7484-49b1-a070-891ea0637664"}
