+# Codex critical current-review remediation
+
+- Plan: `plan03-1`
+- Review kind: `critical-incremental`
+- Continuity base: `5b474d5c1735beb8cca922fd6cc7b6304926df2c`
+- Frozen target: `74ecd4fb64311c69ae0d758d8c1d99b27a9c5572`
+- Source fingerprint:
+  `sha256:df143611ba42181cdfea90c3b205b2c758997dc99817d345256ecea4d9bef078`
+- Scope: complete current target plus the continuous remediation increment
+- External results for this review round: not read; the job has not been submitted
+
+## Review performed
+
+I rechecked the current implementation, tests, configs, schema, PBS launchers,
+Checkers and documentation against every item in the retained
+`critical-current-fs-diloco` disposition. I traced syncer admission and ingest
+composition into `LeaderAuthority`, static replacement authorization, command
+receipt conflict handling, proposal parsing/adjudication, leader release,
+runtime fault injection and the aggregate acceptance paths. I also checked the
+static/dynamic config normalization boundary, resolved-config serialization,
+schema version ownership, public invocation surface, content/path inventories
+and the four-lane reviewer runner.
+
+During the Codex review, two test-boundary omissions were found before this
+target was frozen: the validation suite still named deleted `tests/test_cli.py`,
+and the first composition test exercised receipt conflict propagation but not
+the proposal branch. The stale path was deleted and a valid proposal ingest
+conflict test was added. Both changes are part of this target.
+
+## Disposition verification
+
+- FSD-H1 through H4 remain closed. JUnit all-pass counts, scenario-derived
+  exact fault expectations, durable `last_update_id` resume authority and valid
+  mutation fixtures are all present.
+- FSD-M1 is addressed by real `LeaderAuthority` static-admission composition
+  and separate receipt/proposal integrity propagation tests.
+- FSD-M2 is addressed without weakening authority: the multi-node oracles claim
+  successor advancement and exclusive publication only, while stale
+  fence/token rejection remains independently owned by unit evidence.
+- FSD-M3 and M4 are addressed by file-relative non-vacuous discovery plus
+  tracked path/content inventories with the two intentional versioned wire
+  types as the exact allowed set.
+- FSD-M5 and M6 are addressed by fail-fast schema/command/token exceptions and
+  one launcher-owned takeover boundary propagated unchanged to rank execution
+  and the Checker.
+- FSD-M7 and FSD-L1 through L6 are addressed by deleting the dispatcher,
+  console scripts and protocol re-export facade; using `RunPaths`; removing the
+  unwritten epoch state; aligning Python 3.13; using neutral defaults;
+  propagating release failure; and deriving static membership counts from the
+  sole `sync.num_learners` input without inert scaling fields.
+- FSD-L7 remains informational. `CycleReceiptV1` and
+  `FullUpdateProposalV2` remain intentional independently versioned wire
+  formats, not product-generation surfaces.
+
+## Multi-agent workflow and static gates
+
+The temporary Codex-only policy is removed from current state. The runner now
+owns exactly Claude Opus 5, GLM-5.2, DeepSeek V4 Flash and MiniMax M3, with no
+Kimi alias. Schema-2 Codex review artifacts no longer encode
+`skipped-by-user`; external summaries and dispositions are separate
+best-effort evidence, and valid external findings remain blocking inputs.
+
+Ruff format/lint, Python compilation, all PBS/shell syntax checks, literal PBS
+group checks, diff whitespace checks, source ancestry and a clean formal source
+fingerprint passed on the control plane. Project tests have intentionally not
+run on the login node; they remain gated on current-round external disposition
+and then one-node compute validation.
+
+No open Critical, High, Medium or Low source/test-design finding remains in the
+frozen target. It is approved for external multi-agent review and, subject to
+that disposition, compute-node validation.
+
+Verdict: APPROVE
